  },
  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/carvera.cps`: after `M6 T..`, the Carvera now writes `G0 Z<ClearancePlane|RetractPlane>` (never below the move's Z) before the first `G0 X.. Y..`. This is the same order as at a program start. The X/Y-first branch (`changedAt`) is removed. The provenance header and the note before `xyFirst` cite the firmware source.\n- `crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance.rs`: the X/Y-first case is removed. Two new pins:\n  - `the_carvera_states_the_clearance_before_any_xy_after_its_m6`\n  - `the_carvera_script_cites_where_its_m6_leaves_the_spindle` (replaces `the_carvera_script_names_the_open_hazard_after_its_tool_change`)\n- `docs/decisions/1616-carvera-after-m6.md`: the decision, the sources and the options that were dropped. It supersedes the Carvera part of `docs/decisions/1616-first-traverse-clearance.md` (PR #1632).\n\n## Sources (public GPL source, behaviour only; no vendor binaries, no decompiling)\n\n- MakeraInc/CarveraFirmware `6e12557cfa5eff446bb5fe014354eaa03abf0caa`, `src/modules/tools/atc/ATCHandler.cpp`, `on_main_loop`: at the end of `M6`, the firmware does a machine rapid to `Z = coordinate.clearance_z`, then a rapid to the X/Y that it saved when `M6` arrived. The spindle is not left over the tool rack.\n- Carvera-Community/Carvera_Community_Firmware `2c97111cb0bbd6d3edfac2c138963c0255248865`: the same order.\n- `Robot.cpp`: the soft Z limit is on by default and halts the machine. A `G0 Z` that cannot be reached stops the program.\n- https://wiki.makera.com/en/supported-codes, https://carvera-community.gitbook.io/docs/firmware/supported-commands/mcodes/tool-change, https://github.com/infinitask/carvera-examples/blob/main/docs/carvera-firmware-upgrades.md\n\n## Goldens: NOT regenerated (maintainer decides)\n\nThe brief does not let this PR regenerate NC goldens. These suites are red on this head until the goldens are regenerated:\n- `camcraft-post --test script_carvera`: 5 fail\n- `camcraft-app --test carvera_post`: `a_two_tool_pocket_posts_in_the_carveras_own_words`\n- `camcraft-app --test conformance`: `every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact`, `the_synthesized_stream_locks_the_tool_and_spindle_words`\n\nThe 19 files that differ:\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/carvera/`: `arcs.nc`, `drill_retract.nc`, `extreme_coords.nc`, `full_circle.nc`, `full_circle_raw.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/carvera/`: `contour_disc_hole.nc`, `contour_plate_with_hole.nc`, `contour_tangential_lead.nc`, `drill_peck.nc`, `drill_plate.nc`, `face_square_40x40.nc`, `face_square_40x40_stepped.nc`, `pocket_waterline_plate_with_island.nc`, `pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island.nc`, `slot_fullwidth_centerline.nc`, `slot_wide_channel_rows.nc`, `trace_plate_with_hole.nc`, `two_tool_pocket.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_carvera.nc`\n\nThe diff shape is the same in every file: two lines after each `M6` change places. No line is added or removed. `two_tool_pocket.nc` has two `M6` blocks; all other files have one.\n\n```\n M7\n-G0 X5 Y5\n G0 Z5\n+G0 X5 Y5\n G0 X5 Y5 Z5\n```\n\nTo regenerate: `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_carvera` and `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test carvera_post --test conformance`. I did this in the worktree to measure the diff. Then I reverted the files. They are not in this PR.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test first_traverse_clearance`: 8 pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `camcraft-app` suites `carvera_machines`, `coolant_air`, `makera_z1`, `smoothing`, `program_units`, `post_spindle_rule_all`, `probe_no_coolant`, `mcp_units`: pass. `carvera_post` and `conformance` fail only on the stale goldens above.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not run on a real Carvera. The firmware behaviour is read from source, not seen on a machine.\n- A machine with changed soft limits or a changed `coordinate.clearance_z`. The defaults are taken on trust.\n\nChangelog: Carvera post: the first X/Y traverse after an `M6` tool change now comes after a `G0 Z` to the clearance height, not before it (#1616)\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1616\n",
